 "post": {
  "linkedin": "A filling line loses 26.5 hours a week to changeovers. Sequencing the same orders differently halves that.\n\nIn this illustrative week, 12 orders run on one line in four product families, light to dark. Sequenced by due date, the line changes over 11 times, spends 26.5 hours doing it and still ships three orders late.\n\nThe fix is the cost of the switch. Light to dark takes 1.5 hours. Dark back to light needs a 4-hour clean. Run campaigns from light to dark and the same orders need 13 hours of changeovers, with nothing late. A rush order on Wednesday slots into Thursday's campaign without a single extra changeover.\n\nHow does your scheduler pick the sequence today: due date, habit or changeover cost?\n\nInvented numbers, real mechanics. A new planning concept every Tuesday and Thursday.\n\nFull show: The Planning Desk, supply chain news every weekday on Apple Podcasts and Spotify. Links in the first comment.\n\n#productionplanning #scheduling #supplychain #operations",
  "short_title": "Same 12 Orders, Half the Changeover Hours | Production Scheduling",
